From dc4a0c7e7e2b28f95adde731114ddc3eec01ae1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:32:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 150/174] rule-set: a rule set closed while it reads a list
 stops reading it

A remote rule set checked its context before and after the parse of a
downloaded list, not during it: a box closed meanwhile (an in-process
reload: SIGHUP, or an apply of the Go backend of podkop) let the parse of
a big list run to the end beside the new box, which downloads and parses
its own. After a reboot every list starts empty and is downloaded at
once, five at a time: an apply then stacked full parses in memory.

The readers take the context of the rule set: the source format
(domainset.ReadSourceContext) and the text format (ruletext.ReadContext)
look at it every 4096 items, the build of the trie every 4096 nodes, a
binary set reads through a reader that ends with the context, and the
rules are made one at a time. Local rule sets read so too.
